      "title": "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7ff2c05a-5270-5ab6-93c8-92206f99cbae",
      ":question/problem": "Let $\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{b}$ and points the same direction.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{\\mathbf{b}}{|\\mathbf{b}|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\mathbf{b}| &= \\sqrt{(8)^2+(-6)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{100} \\\\\n&= 10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\mathbf{b}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{\\mathbf{b}}{|\\mathbf{b}|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}\\cdot (\\mathbf{b}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{10}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/requires-calculator": false,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
