      ":question/problem": "Let $\\mathbf{n}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{n}$ and points the same direction.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{\\mathbf{n}}{|\\mathbf{n}|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\mathbf{n}| &= \\sqrt{(3)^2+(4)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{25} \\\\\n&= 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\mathbf{n}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{\\mathbf{n}}{|\\mathbf{n}|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot (\\mathbf{n}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
